      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "69ed5697-9227-5842-992c-52ed78bc6cdf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kristian Zahrtmann, Peder Severin Krøyer, Theodor Esbern Philipsen, Ossian Elgström, Christian Krohg, Maria Krøyer, Anna Ancher, Michael Ancher, Laurits Tuxen, Viggo Johansen, Holger Drachmann\n- Organizations: Royal Swedish Academy of Arts, Skagens Museum\n- Groups: Skagen Painters, Danish artistic generation of the late 19th century\n- Places: Skagen, Denmark\n- Concepts: Academicism, Golden Age of Danish Painting, naturalism, realism\n\nFacts:\n- Kristian Zahrtmann was born on 31 March 1843 and died on 22 June 1917.\n- Kristian Zahrtmann was a Danish painter.\n- Kristian Zahrtmann was part of the Danish artistic generation of the late 19th century with Peder Severin Krøyer and Theodor Esbern Philipsen.\n- That late-19th-century Danish artistic generation broke away from traditional Academicism and the heritage of the Golden Age of Danish Painting in favor of naturalism and realism.\n- Peder Severin Krøyer was one of the best known, most beloved, and most colorful members of the Skagen Painters.\n- The Skagen Painters were a community of Danish and Nordic artists who lived, gathered, or worked in Skagen, Denmark, especially during the final decades of the 19th century.\n- Ossian Elgström studied at the Royal Swedish Academy of Arts from 1906 to 1907.\n- Ossian Elgström studied with Kristian Zahrtmann in 1907 and with Christian Krohg in 1908.\n- Skagens Museum identifies Maria Krøyer, P. S. Krøyer, Anna Ancher, Michael Ancher, Laurits Tuxen, Viggo Johansen, and Holger Drachmann as important artists.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7da03b4d-7871-5f43-bc42-95a4b6254267",
        "text": "Page: Kristian Zahrtmann. Sentence: Peder Henrik Kristian Zahrtmann, known as Kristian Zahrtmann, (31 March 1843 – 22 June 1917) was a Danish painter.\nPage: Kristian Zahrtmann. Sentence: He was a part of the Danish artistic generation in the late 19th century, along with Peder Severin Krøyer and Theodor Esbern Philipsen, who broke away from both the strictures of traditional Academicism and the heritage of the Golden Age of Danish Painting, in favor of naturalism and realism.\nPage: Peder Severin Krøyer. Sentence: He is one of the best known and beloved, and the most colorful of the Skagen Painters, a community of Danish and Nordic artists who lived, gathered, or worked in Skagen, Denmark, especially during the final decades of the 19th century.\nPage: Ossian Elgström. Sentence: Elgström studied at the Royal Swedish Academy of Arts from 1906 to 1907, and then with Kristian Zahrtmann in 1907 and with Christian Krohg in 1908.\nPage: Skagens Museum. Sentence: Important artists include Maria and P. S. Krøyer, Anna and Michael Ancher, Laurits Tuxen, Viggo Johansen and Holger Drachmann.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
